## Summary

I built a production-polished, native Apple (SwiftUI) implementation of **`VehicleSettingsTab`** at parity with `features/vehicles/components/VehicleSettingsTab.tsx`, following the established `RegionSettings` convention exactly. Delivered **12 files** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/VehicleSettingsTab.*`):

- **Adapter** (pure core): 6-key descriptor catalog, RFC3339⇄Date helpers, `effectiveToDraft`/`parseDraft` validation, source discriminator, a11y builders
- **Model / Seams**: `VehicleSettingsTabSource` seam (P1/S8), projection, `@Observable` model with per-row save/reset pending + stale auto-refresh, telemetry (P1/S11) + toast seams, in-memory source, i18n facade (P1/S10)
- **Views / Row / Copy**: glass-panel header + freshness chip, per-key editor rows (text / select / datetime inputs), source pills, validation, Save/Reset, and loading/empty/error chrome
- **Previews**, **strings**, **Tests + ModelTests** (42 tests)

**All states reproduced**: loading, empty, error+retry, data (6 rows), stale, offline. Full a11y labels, Dynamic Type, reduce-motion. Every web i18n key mapped.

